## Clues
1-2. A young hawk. ~ NIAS
3-4. What Samson did to the Philistines. ~ SLEW
5-6. A farm implement ~ PLOW
7-8. An ensign. ~ FLAG
9-10. A small amphibious animal. ~ FROG
11-12. To kill. ~ SLAY
13-14. That which is here present. ~ THIS
15-16. It revolves arount the earth. ~ MOON
17-18. A cavity. ~ HOLE
19-20. Autumn time. ~ FALL
21-22. Concern. ~ CARE
23-24. What you do when you don't win. ~ LOSE
25-26. A boat with a flat bottom. ~ FLATBOAT
27-28. To apprehend. ~ ARREST
29-30. Part of your face ~ NOSE
31-32. Myself. ~ ME
33-34. To have existence. ~ BE
35-36. An infernal machine. ~ BOMB
37-38. A little stream. ~ RUNLET
39-40. A measure. ~ METEYARD
41-42. Sold by butchers. ~ MEAT
43-44. A yellow metal. ~ GOLD
45-46. Detained. ~ KEPT
47-48. Ten cents. ~ DIME
49-50. A crytogamous plant. ~ MOSS
51-52. What every one does to prolong life. ~ EATS
53-54. A highway. ~ ROAD
55-56. To haul. ~ DRAW
57-58. Beloved by all Irishmen. ~ ERIN
59-60. To be acquainted with. ~ KNOW
61-62. To prepare for publication. ~ EDIT
63-64. Enough. ~ ENOW
65-66. A musical instrument. ~ TROMBONE
67-68. Becoming. ~ BESEEMLY
69-3. A verb. ~ IS
70-5. A lofty mountain. ~ ALP
71-18. Used in the garden. ~ HOE
72-16. Not out. ~ IN
2-7. Anything considered as having a distinct personality. ~ SELF
4-9. A ferocious animal. ~ WOLF
6-11. Physical conflicts between nations. ~ WARS
8-25. An outdoor game ~ GOLF
10-27. A festivity. ~ GALA
12-29. Something a sailor loves to spin. ~ YARN
23-30. To let slip. ~ LOSE
21-28. A garment. ~ COAT
19-26. To abstain from food. ~ FAST
17-24. A long eared rodent. ~ HARE
15-22. A birthmark. ~ MOLE
13-20. To strike a bell slowly. ~ TOLL
35-42. A large cask. ~ BUTT
37-44. What FUN is. ~ READ
39-46. To reduce from a solid to a liquid state by heat. ~ MELT
41-48. To be gloomy. ~ MOPE
43-50. Precious stones. ~ GEMS
45-52. An affectionate salutation. ~ KISS
47-74. A tiny mark. ~ DOT
49-73. Mother. ~ MA
36-53. To sustain. ~ BEAR
38-55. The past perfect of tread. ~ TROD
40-57. A challenge. ~ DARE
54-59. Not light. ~ DARK
56-61. Fermented grape juice. ~ WINE
58-63. A knob. ~ NODE
60-75. To gain. ~ WIN
62-76. Toward. ~ TO


